==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:Bouguereau-The First Mourning-1888.jpg|thumb|William Adolphe Bouguereau's ''The First Mourning'' (1888)]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|Abel}}, from {{der|en|la|Abel}}, from {{der|en|grc|Ἅβελ}}, from {{der|en|hbo|הֶבֶל||breath, vapor; vanity|tr=heḇel}}, possibly from {{der|en|akk|𒌉𒍑|tr=ablu|t=son}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈeɪ.bl̩/|lang=en}}
* {{homophones|lang=en|able}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{lb|en|biblical character}} The son of [[Adam]] and [[Eve]] who was killed by his brother [[Cain]].
#* {{RQ:Authorized Version|Genesis|4|8}}
#*: And Cain talked with '''Abel''' his brother: and it came to pass, when they were in the field, that Cain rose up against '''Abel''' his brother, and slew him.
# {{given name|male|lang=en|from=Hebrew}}.
# {{surname|en|patronymic|from=given names}}

